{"name":"Silken Raspberry","hex":"#aa7d89","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"silken","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Made of silk.","Synonym of silky, like silk, silklike, particularly\nHaving a smooth, soft, or light texture.\n\nSuave.\n\n Having a smooth, soft, or flowing utterance; attractive or  convincing through pleasing expression."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To render silken or silklike."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/silken"},{"term":"raspberry","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The plant Rubus idaeus.","Any of many other (but not all) species in the genus Rubus."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Containing or having the flavor/flavour of raspberries.","Of a dark pinkish red."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/raspberry"}],"entries":[{"title":"Silk","blocks":[{"text":"Silk is a natural protein fiber, some forms of which can be woven or knitted into textiles. The protein fiber of silk is composed mainly of fibroin (75-80%) and a smaller coating of sericin (20-25%). It is most commonly produced from the cocoons of certain insect larvae. The best-known silk is obtained from the cocoons of the larvae of the mulberry silkworm Bombyx mori, which are reared in captivity (sericulture)."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2e/Silk_raw_01a.jpg/330px-Silk_raw_01a.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Silk","wikidata":"Q37681"},{"title":"Raspberry","blocks":[{"text":"The raspberry is the edible fruit of several plant species in the genus Rubus of the rose family, most of which are in the subgenus Idaeobatus. The name also applies to these plants themselves. Raspberries are perennial with woody stems."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Raspberry_-_halved_%28Rubus_idaeus%29.jpg/330px-Raspberry_-_halved_%28Rubus_idaeus%29.jpg?utm_source=en.